  "result": "The 10-minute lesson on O3 is written, with a quiz and key to go with it. I haven't opened the lesson in a browser or checked its length with a script.\n\n- **Lesson:** `lessons/0001-context-and-memory.html` (about 1,500 words, as the 10-minute budget needs). It's example-first, built on the makerspace assistant. It covers:\n  - the context window, with a trace of how the context grows call by call;\n  - what survives between steps and between sessions;\n  - retrieval and notes, with one worked example and a sorting exercise.\n  The lesson also has a recall warm-up, a short practice check, a summary and links to its sources.\n- **Quiz:** `quizzes/0002.json` has five items, with the key in `keys/0002.json`. None of the items repeat the lesson's practice. Ask me when you want to take it, and I'll give hints rather than answers.\n- **Sources:** I added Anthropic's context-engineering essay (the primary source), the context-windows docs and the memory-tool docs to `RESOURCES.md`. The search only returned excerpts of the essay, not its full text, so I only used points those excerpts supported.\n- **Gaps:** the Wisdom section of `RESOURCES.md` is empty because I haven't vetted a community for agent builders yet.\n- **Notes:** I recorded the lesson and quiz in `NOTES.md`.\n\nAsk me about anything in the lesson that's unclear. Do you want a cheat sheet on what to keep in context, retrieve or save as a note?",
